      "id": "stars",
      "name": "Stars",
      "description": "Small hard-edged points, most of them round and a few drawn out into a short cross. They are thickest right along the topline - the dorsal third of the barrel, the croup, and the crest of the neck rather than the whole upper half of it - and thin steadily going down, out to nothing by the belly and by the knee and hock. They clump on top of that: a starred horse has three or four patches where the points crowd, not an even dusting.",
